# Issue 670: inherited descriptor survives the existing OSH launcher
Date: 2026-10-23. Host: AArch64 Linux (spark-b87b). Binary: build/osh/osh sha256 410bcec62d1ba1e6cb5c4ec6172e71eeabe158fd784a8bf0f7a7f352f02ad83e (before fix, rebuilt from the commit's source).
Source: src/osh/host/osh_exec.c sha256 5001ceba594da08874436d5f4622326118d7453cb180d96c8029d04204acd735 (before fix).

Policy (no read grant at all):
    principal 1
    allow spawn /bin/sh

Command:
    ./build/osh/osh --caps policy-noread --journal journal2 \
        -c '/bin/sh -c "cat <&9"' 9</etc/hostname

Result: exit 0, stdout is the protected file contents:
    spark-b87b

The child was never granted a read capability. The parent's descriptor 9 was
opened before OSH and survived fork/exec because the child closed only the
descriptors OSH knew about.

Second probe (read grant present) shows the descriptor table seen by the child:
    ./build/osh/osh --caps policy --journal journal \
        -c '/bin/sh -c "echo FDS:; ls -l /proc/self/fd"' 9</etc/hostname

    FDS:
    total 0
    lrwx------ 1 ... 0 -> /dev/null
    l-wx------ 1 ... 1 -> .../inherited.out
    lrwx------ 1 ... 16 -> /dev/pts/2
    lrwx------ 1 ... 18 -> /dev/pts/2
    l-wx------ 1 ... 2 -> .../inherited.err
    lr-x------ 1 ... 3 -> /proc/466486/fd
    lr-x------ 1 ... 9 -> /etc/hostname

Descriptors 16 and 18 are also embedder-inherited and reached the child.
